*> reject-at: 2014 2023
*> ISO 1989:2023 14.9.39.3 SR20, last sentence - "The function-prototypes associated with identifier-12 and
*> identifier-13 shall have the same signature." FPD is restricted to NSDBL (one USING formal) and FPZ to
*> NSZERO (none), so neither the pointer-to-pointer copy nor the ADDRESS OF FUNCTION sender conforms.
*> COBOLNET1959 (the one code SR20 and SR22 share - kb/Work PB817). kb/Work PB452.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
FUNCTION-ID. NSDBL.
DATA DIVISION.
LINKAGE SECTION.
01 L-ARG PIC S9(4).
01 L-RES PIC S9(9).
PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-ARG RETURNING L-RES.
    COMPUTE L-RES = L-ARG * 2
    GOBACK.
END FUNCTION NSDBL.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
FUNCTION-ID. NSZERO.
DATA DIVISION.
LINKAGE SECTION.
01 L-RES PIC S9(9).
PROCEDURE DIVISION RETURNING L-RES.
    MOVE 0 TO L-RES
    GOBACK.
END FUNCTION NSZERO.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. NEGFP04.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
CONFIGURATION SECTION.
REPOSITORY.
    FUNCTION NSDBL
    FUNCTION NSZERO.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01 FPD USAGE FUNCTION-POINTER TO NSDBL.
01 FPZ USAGE FUNCTION-POINTER TO NSZERO.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
MAIN.
    SET FPD TO FPZ
    STOP RUN.
END PROGRAM NEGFP04.
